      "id": 1,
      "text": "Weedsport got its original name, Weed's Basin, because a canal basin turned boats around during the Erie Canal era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weedsport%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village officially became incorporated in 1831, marking its formal start as a community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weedsport%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Erie Canal once cut through Weedsport, but today it runs along the Seneca River a mile north of the village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weedsport%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Weedsport sits where New York State Routes 31 and 34 cross, a historic crossroads for travelers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weedsport%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Centreport Aqueduct, a relic of canal engineering, earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places in 2000.",
